(7413925, 1168236, 59029, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club!<br/> <br/>Hah, all that''s missing are some ps''d in red eyes :-)  Artistically, I wonder if the name Cerberus simply didn''t register with voters as the (traditionally) tri-headed dog guardian to the gates of Hell, hence his downward gaze to the lower two-thirds where the grass is just a little bit lighter as though aglow with flame.  I like the tones you got with the allowed b/w conversion.<br/> <br/>Technically it''s an OK shot, nothing outstanding in terms of lighting or comp.  Pity it was a Minimal challenge, cloning out the harness and/or the leash may have helped to isolate the dog a bit more and possibly add some menace to their expression - who knows what a loose dog might do?  Basically does meet the challenge descrip though.  I think some voters may have forgotten that Minimal is very restrictive in terms of what you can do both in camera and post.<br/> <br/>Sorry this hasn''t been the most in-depth critique, hope it helps.<br/> <br/>Susan</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club! Hah, all that''s missing are some ps''d in red eyes :-)  Artistically, I wonder if the name Cerberus simply didn''t register with voters as the (traditionally) tri-headed dog guardian to the gates of Hell, hence his downward gaze to the lower two-thirds where the grass is just a little bit lighter as though aglow with flame.  I like the tones you got with the allowed b/w conversion. Technically it''s an OK shot, nothing outstanding in terms of lighting or comp.  Pity it was a Minimal challenge, cloning out the harness and/or the leash may have helped to isolate the dog a bit more and possibly add some menace to their expression - who knows what a loose dog might do?  Basically does meet the challenge descrip though.  I think some voters may have forgotten that Minimal is very restrictive in terms of what you can do both in camera and post. Sorry this hasn''t been the most in-depth critique, hope it helps. Susan', '2015-11-03 18:57:48.000000', NULL, 0),
(7415291, 1168156, 16912, '<td valign="top">Andi here from the Critique Club.<br/> <br/>I did consider writing this backwards but after <b><i>.bulc euqitirc eht morf ereh idna</i></b> I considered it hard work for me and the your ;)<br/> <br/>I often feel minimal editing challenges bring out the best in people photographically but it can oft do the reverse. In this case the only thing I think this image lacks is a little contrast and sharpness. Composition is spot on and the cement truck is a fantastic subject for the challenge (serendipity or planned?).<br/> <br/>I''m surprised it didn''t finish higher.<br/> <br/></td>', 'Andi here from the Critique Club. I did consider writing this backwards but after .bulc euqitirc eht morf ereh idna I considered it hard work for me and the your ;) I often feel minimal editing challenges bring out the best in people photographically but it can oft do the reverse. In this case the only thing I think this image lacks is a little contrast and sharpness. Composition is spot on and the cement truck is a fantastic subject for the challenge (serendipity or planned?). I''m surprised it didn''t finish higher. ', '2015-11-09 18:25:37.000000', NULL, 0),
(7540866, 1168199, 117467, '<td valign="top">Lydia, Sorry to hear this and hope that your experience has remedied the procedure''s underlying cause(s). Be well :) and hope you can get all of your boys back again soon, and under happier circumstances.<br/> <br/>Sorry too, in learning about the BS DQ. Another example of why from the sidelines I only silently root for you all in what seems like an array of bewildering constraints. <br/> <br/>The unspoken art in ''Boys will be Boys'', and other BS DQs, is navigation of a system of rules that generally remain unseen and which I''ve never understood. God''s speed to all of you that do!<br/> <br/></td>', 'Lydia, Sorry to hear this and hope that your experience has remedied the procedure''s underlying cause(s). Be well :) and hope you can get all of your boys back again soon, and under happier circumstances. Sorry too, in learning about the BS DQ. Another example of why from the sidelines I only silently root for you all in what seems like an array of bewildering constraints.  The unspoken art in ''Boys will be Boys'', and other BS DQs, is navigation of a system of rules that generally remain unseen and which I''ve never understood. God''s speed to all of you that do! ', '2017-10-25 11:09:35.000000', NULL, 0);
